  "published": "2026-08-25T20:14:18.117Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.4.0 — New: H264StreamingSession connects Kiln.RateControl to the encoder. Feed it EncoderNetworkFeedback per frame and it applies slice QP, a per-picture bit budget, recovery IDRs and live speed-mode changes; ChangeResolution handles resolution switches. Deterministic — wall-clock is a caller-supplied input, never measured internally, so identical frames plus identical feedback give an identical bitstream. Also public: ApplySpeedMode/ApplySpeedKnobs for live reconfiguration and EncodeFrame(targetBitsPerFrame:) for per-picture budgets. Reference count is now adjustable per frame below the SPS-signalled maximum with no IDR required. Not implemented and documented as such: intra refresh (surfaced as a request, never faked), frame scaling (the caller supplies frames at the decided resolution), and frame pacing/dropping. Includes the 0.3.1 deblocking conformance fix — if you are on 0.3.0 or earlier and use AdaptiveQuantStrength or TargetBitsPerFrame, upgrading is recommended.",
